title: Microsoft Hyper-V VM: Dynamic virtual disk
agents: windows
catalog: os/storage
license: GPLv2
distribution: check_mk
description:
 This check monitors the size of the image file of a dynamic or differencing
 virtual disk of a virtual machine running on Microsoft Hyper-V. It shows the
 file name, the file size, the maximum size of the disk and the type.

 Levels for the file size are configured with the rule "Hyper-V VM VHD",
 as an absolute value or relative to the maximum size of the disk. There are
 no levels by default.

 Fixed disks are monitored by the check {hyperv_vm_vhd_fixed}.

 The data is collected by the agent plug-in {hyperv_host.ps1}, which can be
 deployed with the agent bakery rule "Hyper-V". The plug-in sends the data
 as piggyback data to a host with the name of the VM.

item:
 The controller type, the controller number and the location of the disk,
 for example {SCSI 0 1}.

discovery:
 One service is created for each dynamic or differencing virtual disk.
